#!/usr/bin/env python3
# Generated by Claudian.
"""JARVIS Web — FastAPI backend for the browser front end.

JARVIS had no HTTP surface at all: the Electron app talks to it over IPC by
spawning the Python process. That works for one desktop app and nothing else.
This exposes the same brain over HTTP + WebSocket so any browser can drive it.

What it serves
--------------
  GET  /                  the front end
  GET  /api/status        health, models, DB counts, fallback tiers
  GET  /api/skills        all registered skills
  POST /api/command       run a command, get JARVIS's reply
  GET  /api/events        recent conversation history (SQLite)
  GET  /api/facts         remembered facts
  POST /api/facts         remember something
  DELETE /api/facts/{id}  forget a fact
  GET  /api/search        full-text search across facts + events\n  POST /api/transcribe    speech to text (Electron cannot use the browser API)\n  GET  /api/brain         what JARVIS has learned\n  POST /api/brain/learn   run a learning cycle now
  WS   /ws                live state stream that drives the visualiser

Design notes
------------
Speech happens in the *browser* (Web Speech API), not through the desktop TTS.
Two processes fighting over the speakers is worse than either alone, and it
keeps this server headless — it can run over SSH or on another machine.

Run:
    python3 web/server.py          # http://127.0.0.1:8420
    python3 web/server.py --port 9000 --host 0.0.0.0
"""

